<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49629" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ūfens</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Oufens</span></b> , ap. <i><span class="en">Fest. p. 194</span></i> Müll.),
			entis, m.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A small river in Latium</i>, <i>that
				flows past Tarracina</i>, now <i>Ufente</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				3, 5, 9, § 60</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 7,
				802</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 8, 383</span></i>.— Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ūfentīnus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Oufent-</span></b> ), a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the Ufens</i>, <i>Ufentine</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tribus,</span>”
				<i>one of the thirty-five Roman tribes</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					9, 20, 6</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
			194</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A man's name</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 7,
				745</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 4,
			339</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4,
		343</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
